ch faith is there in green  hydrogen globally and will it pay off  well joining me now uh is rice says  energy head of hydrogen research mikoi  Lee thank you very much for joining us  so do you think there's a future then in  green hydrogen  definitely uh first of all thank you  very much for having me on your show uh  and well I think that definitely there  is a future for green hydrogen in the  world of energy transition and as well  as decarbonization  how do you think it will be used if it's  made on this mask  so there's actually a lot of ways that  hydrogen can be used is actually being  used around the world at the moment and  one of the key use if we look into the  future is of course to make nitrogen  based higher fertilizers to support our  food industry other uses uh including  you know fuel for transportation  feedstock for steel production as well  as for our generation as well so there's  a lot of use that you can make out of  green hydrogen and it's often being  tooted it's one of the key pillars of  the energy transition  are you excited by this project because  the big argument around green hydrogen  is that it's really expensive  yes I think uh if we look back in the  days of Renewables of solar and when  they were all very expensive back then  but because there are push from the  government push from companies they have  been decreased their costs and we  believe the same thing will happen for  green hydrogen in the Futures so that  means it will get cheaper and but app  for every new technologies this will  start out expensive and we need to put a  lot of efforts into it in order to start  reducing the cost to be used in the  future as well personally I'm very  excited about this project that is  happening in Egypt it is actually among  a lot of other projects that has been  announced over the past few months  leading up to cop 27 we have companies  own around the world looking to invest  into each to make green hydrogen and for  anyone that doesn't know of course green  hydrogen is hydrogen made from renewable  energy  okay thank you very much interesting to  your thoughts uh Ming coily thank you so  much for joining us  now you can get to all the latest news  from cop27 on our live blog so just make  sure you scan the QR code on the screen  right now and uh just before we go a  reminder that our weekly climate Show  with Tom Heap it's back and you can  watch it on Saturdays and Sundays at 3  30 in the afternoon or at 7 30 in the  evening  and of course we'd love more questions  actually from you you can scan the QR  code here or you can go to any of our  social media accounts and put your  questions in the comments and Tom will  answer some of your questions in his  show  that's all from us today join us  tomorrow for the very latest from cop27  and the rest of the news affecting the  planets
 

